<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-19878] Restrict possibility to create two caches with the same schema and index name</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-19878</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;It&#8217;s possible to create two different caches with the same schema and index name inside it from a client and after that get a failing of the server node during start-up with the error &quot;Duplicate index name... &quot; during start caches.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;scenario:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;start at least two server nodes&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;start client node which creates two different caches during start-up (via setting cache configs to config of client node) with the same schema name and index name, it leads to crushing the cluster&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;then try to start the cluster and get the error &quot;Duplicate index name...&quot;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="13541896">IGNITE-19878</key>
